## Progress (2026-10-25)

The first block implementation is in 900-NRL-0003's backend spike. This task adds the stored-reference comparisons, independent finite differences for every input/trainable parameter, knot/tail checks, malformed artifact checks, exact round trips, and explicit buffer/overflow checks. The initial run had ten passing host tests; the final eleven-test check follows staging on fast-test, on the NRL branch only. No acceptance checkbox is closed on the strength of the added test alone.

## Resolution

- The branch's dense SiLU and linear-spline gated block implementations are checked by `nrl/crates/nrl-lab/tests/numerics.rs` against externally generated PyTorch outputs, input/parameter gradients and a one-step training result.
- Independent finite differences exercise every input and trainable parameter away from knots. Separate checks cover exact knots, both tails, finite values, buffer lengths, overflow, malformed/oversized/versioned artifacts, unknown/duplicate fields, no-overwrite and exact round trips.
- After staging the built branch in fast-test (`cb3fb7da`), `bash nrl/tools/check.sh` passed on the **NRL branch** at `3d820f72`: **11 Rust tests**, release rlibs for x86_64-unknown-none and aarch64-unknown-none-softfloat, and the two-case host demonstration. No build or test ran on fast-test. Full output: `nrl/reports/rust-check-2026-10-25.txt`.
- Maximum recorded reference error was 5.551115123125783e-17. The dense synthetic MSE moved from 0.10231179736197876 to 0.09556269780699116; the spline MSE from 0.15264958541547757 to 0.12677966117930756. These are different fixed test blocks, not a quality/compression comparison or held-out model result.
- `nrl/reports/cpu-f64-2026-10-25.json` records the profile and limitations. The rest of T03 (pruned, cubic Hermite, SVD), general T04 import/export and T11 remain open under 900. Code landing and CI wiring are pending.
